# Do not put service secrets here.
#
# Local dev — copy each service layer's .env.example:
#   identity/frontend/.env.example → identity/frontend/.env
#   identity/backend/.env.example  → identity/backend/.env
#   (same pattern for webonone-v2, media, email, data, sms, payment, website)
#
# Production (IIS) — one file at repo root (not this file):
#   copy production.env.example production.env
#   edit production.env, then npm run deploy:<service>
#   (deploy runs npm run env:apply and writes each service's backend/.env + frontend/.env.production)
#
# Local dev ports (strict — each service fails if its port is taken):
#   WebOnOne  FE 3010  BE 4010
#   Identity  FE 3011  BE 4011
#   UI Kit    FE 3012  (showcase only)
#   Media     FE 3013  BE 4013
#   Email     FE 3014  BE 4014
#   Data      FE 3015  BE 4015
